{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"frousy-head-bee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The cache-ineffective warning cannot tell 'model does not cache' from 'prompt below the cacheable floor'\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:warn_if_cache_ineffective` (story 2932) warns when prompt caching was requested but both counters are zero:\n\n```python\nif (caching_requested\n        and usage.get('cache_read_tokens', 0) == 0\n        and usage.get('cache_write_tokens', 0) == 0\n        and usage.get('input_tokens', 0) > 0):\n```\n\nIt was added for a REAL defect: `opus-4-5` reports both counters zero while billing the full input, with no provider error. That defect is worth catching.\n\nBut the predicate has no lower bound, and the codebase ALREADY KNOWS there is one: `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:45` defines `CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS = 4096` — 'the minimum prompt-prefix the anthropic cache will write/read (Opus 4.8 floor). Below this the parent-plan system prefix never caches.'\n\n**Below 4096 tokens, zero/zero is the CORRECT and EXPECTED result, not a symptom.** The warning fires anyway and asserts the operator 'is paying full input price on every call' — which is true but not actionable, because no configuration change could make a sub-floor prompt cache.\n\n## Observed (this session, both providers)\n\nEvery warning observed fired well under the floor:\n\n| run | model | input_tokens | warned |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| plan-review 281f (direct Anthropic) | `claude-sonnet-4-6` | 2184 | yes |\n| plan-review 281f (direct Anthropic) | `claude-opus-4-8` | 1822 – 3140 (≈20 calls) | yes, each |\n| plan-review 281f (Bedrock) | `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` | 2184, 2317 | yes |\n\n**The decisive observation:** in the Bedrock run the aggregate usage for the same review was `cache_write_tokens: 2132`, `cache_read_tokens: 0` — i.e. caching DID engage in that run, on the call whose prefix cleared the floor — while the per-call warnings for the smaller calls simultaneously claimed caching 'had NO effect'. The warning therefore contradicts the run's own aggregate telemetry.\n\nA single `rebar review-plan` emits roughly twenty of these lines.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n1. **Alarm fatigue on the one signal that catches silent cost bleed.** The warning's whole justification is that an ineffective cache is invisible without it. Firing ~20 times per gate run, almost always benignly, trains operators to filter it out — so when a model genuinely stops caching (the opus-4-5 case), the signal is already noise.\n2. **It gets louder exactly at the cutover.** Post-Bedrock every gate run emits these, and they name the Bedrock model, so they will read as 'Bedrock broke caching' during precisely the window when the team is watching for Bedrock regressions. That is a false lead planted at the worst moment.\n3. It contradicts the run's own aggregate usage numbers, which undermines trust in the telemetry generally.\n\n## Approach (candidate, not a decision)\n\nGate the warning on the floor: only warn when `input_tokens >= CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS`, so it fires only where caching COULD have worked and demonstrably did not. The constant currently lives in `plan_review/pass1.py` while the warning lives in `llm/structured_run.py`, so it needs a shared home (`capabilities.py` or `config.py`) rather than a second literal — the epic already has one hand-synced duplicated constant (`DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID`) and should not add another.\n\nConsider also aggregating per RUN rather than per CALL: 'this run made N cacheable-size calls and none cached' is the actionable statement; a per-call line is not.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a test asserts NO warning is emitted when `caching_requested` and both counters are zero but `input_tokens` is below the floor\n- [ ] a test asserts the warning IS still emitted above the floor with both counters zero (the opus-4-5 defect it exists for stays caught)\n- [ ] the floor constant has ONE definition shared by `pass1.py` and `structured_run.py`, not a second literal\n- [ ] [operator-attested] a full `rebar review-plan` run emits zero cache warnings when caching is working, evidenced by the run's aggregate `cache_write_tokens > 0`","id":"7a79-a920-afe7-40cf","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"warn_if_cache_ineffective ignores the 4096-token cache floor and false-alarms on every small call"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785443974733815001,"uuid":"6852ce1e-ceab-4708-bdc0-9cad73a58b85"}